{# Landing page for the YAIkes browser extension.

   Built from the Claude Design handoff (design_handoff_landing). Tokens,
   spacing and copy follow it; the page carries its own scoped stylesheet
   because the design deliberately has NO border-radius, a two-font semantic
   split and a paper-on-clay palette, none of which the site's article styles
   provide. Everything is scoped under .yk- so it cannot leak into the rest of
   the site.

   THREE DEPARTURES FROM THE HANDOFF, all because the reference described a
   product that does not exist:

   1. Every open-source claim is gone — the hero overline, the "Source on
      GitHub" and "View source" buttons, the nav GitHub link, the §5 "open
      source" column and the "MIT licence" footer. The repository is private
      and its LICENSE reserves all rights. Publishing "MIT licence" on a page
      about proprietary software is a false statement about the terms someone
      receives it under, and it appeared in five places. Reinstating it is a
      real option — but it is a decision about the licence, not about the page.

   2. "Your icks live in local extension storage you can export or wipe" —
      there is no export. Wiping is real (per-rule Reset, and uninstalling),
      exporting is not.

   3. The screenshots come from the extension's own E2E suite rather than from
      the handoff's copies. The handoff's popup shot predates the removal of
      the paid tier and still shows a licence field, so shipping it would
      advertise a control the product no longer has.

   The Chrome Web Store URL does not exist yet. Until it does, the CTAs say so
   rather than linking nowhere — see `yaikesStoreUrl` below. #}

{% set yaikesStoreUrl = "" %}
{% set supportUrl = "https://buymeacoffee.com/kamilandrzejrybacki" %}

<style>
  /* ---- tokens ---------------------------------------------------------- */
  .yk {
    --paper: #fdfcfa;
    --clay: #e8e6e1;
    --ink: #1a1917;
    --body: #4a4741;
    --muted: #6f6b64;
    --faint: #8a857c;
    --ochre: oklch(0.62 0.13 60);
    --ochre-deep: oklch(0.52 0.10 62);
    --ochre-light: oklch(0.75 0.11 62);
    --slate: oklch(0.62 0.06 240);
    --slate-text: oklch(0.52 0.06 240);
    --hair: rgba(26, 25, 23, 0.12);
    --hair-strong: rgba(26, 25, 23, 0.16);
    --chrome: #f2f0ec;
    --sans: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    --mono: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  /* The site's base layout centres everything in a narrow container; this page
     is full-bleed clay with its own column, so it steps outside it. */
  body.yaikes-page { background: var(--clay); }
  body.yaikes-page .container { max-width: none; width: 100%; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  /* The site chrome, both ends. base.njk renders its own header for every page
     except Home and articles, and this page has a sticky nav with its own
     wordmark — two site titles stacked, one of them above a nav bar that is
     supposed to be the top of the page. The footer was already hidden here; the
     header was missed because it only appears once deployed, not in the
     standalone preview. */
  body.yaikes-page > .container > .header,
  body.yaikes-page .header { display: none; }
  body.yaikes-page .footer { display: none; }

  .yk {
    background: var(--clay);
    color: var(--body);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .yk *, .yk *::before, .yk *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  .yk-col { width: min(1060px, 100%); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }

  /* No border-radius anywhere. The logo tile and the mascot eyes are the two
     exceptions, and they are the only round things on the page by design. */
  .yk h1, .yk h2, .yk h3, .yk p, .yk ul { margin: 0; }
  .yk a { color: var(--ochre-deep); text-decoration: none;
          border-bottom: 1px solid oklch(0.52 0.10 62 / 0.35); }
  .yk a:hover { color: oklch(0.42 0.11 62); border-bottom-color: oklch(0.42 0.11 62); }
  .yk img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

  /* ---- nav ------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-nav {
    position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10;
    background: var(--clay); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .yk-nav-in { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 18px; height: 62px; }
  .yk-brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; margin-right: auto;
              border: 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .yk-brand:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .yk-logo {
    width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 7px; background: var(--ochre-deep);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 4px; flex: none;
  }
  .yk-logo i { width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff; display: block; }
  .yk-word { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
             font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink); }
  .yk-nav-links { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 20px; }
  .yk-nav-links a { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--body); border: 0; }
  .yk-nav-links a:hover { color: var(--ink); }

  /* ---- buttons --------------------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-btn {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); border: 1px solid transparent;
    background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); padding: 12px 22px; font-size: 14px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .yk-btn:hover { background: var(--ochre-deep); color: var(--paper); border-color: transparent; }
  .yk-btn-sm { padding: 7px 14px; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .yk-btn-out {
    background: none; color: var(--ink); border: 1px solid rgba(26, 25, 23, 0.35);
  }
  .yk-btn-out:hover { background: none; color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); }
  /* A CTA with nowhere to go is not a button. It states the situation instead,
     which is the honest thing to render before the listing is live. */
  .yk-btn-wait {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--faint); border: 1px dashed var(--hair-strong); padding: 12px 22px;
  }
  .yk-btn-wait.yk-btn-sm { padding: 7px 14px; font-size: 12px; }

  /* ---- type ------------------------------------------------------------ */
  .yk-over { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.16em;
             text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); }
  .yk h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 58px); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.03;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em; max-width: 18ch; color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance; margin: 18px 0 20px;
  }
  .yk h2 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 32px); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.15; text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .yk-lead { font-size: 17.5px; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 58ch; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .yk-note { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--faint); }
  .yk-cap { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); margin-top: 12px; }
  .yk-ochre { color: var(--ochre-deep); }
  .yk-slate { color: var(--slate-text); }
  .yk-mono { font-family: var(--mono); }

  /* ---- sections -------------------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-hero { padding-top: 72px; }
  .yk-sec { padding-top: 88px; }
  .yk-label { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.16em;
              text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .yk-ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin-top: 30px; }

  /* ---- screenshot frames ----------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-frame { border: 1px solid var(--hair-strong); background: var(--paper);
              box-shadow: 0 24px 60px -32px rgba(26, 25, 23, 0.35); }
  .yk-frame-sm { box-shadow: 0 18px 48px -28px rgba(26, 25, 23, 0.35); }
  .yk-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; background: var(--chrome);
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); padding: 9px 12px; }
  .yk-dot { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: #cfccc6; display: block; }
  .yk-bar span.yk-mono { margin-left: 10px; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--faint); }

  /* ---- cards ----------------------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-grid3 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
              gap: 18px; margin-top: 26px; }
  .yk-card { background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid rgba(26, 25, 23, 0.14); padding: 24px; }
  .yk-card h3 { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin: 14px 0 8px; }
  .yk-card p { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .yk-dia { width: 12px; height: 12px; transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .yk-dia-fill { background: var(--ochre); }
  .yk-dia-out { border: 1.5px solid var(--slate); }
  .yk-circles { display: flex; gap: 5px; }
  .yk-circles i { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%;
                  border: 1.5px solid var(--slate); display: block; }

  /* ---- two-column sections --------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
            gap: 36px; align-items: center; margin-top: 26px; }
  .yk-two p { font-size: 16px; margin-top: 16px; max-width: 52ch; }

  /* ---- privacy panel --------------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-dark { background: var(--ink); color: rgba(253, 252, 250, 0.75); padding: 40px; }
  .yk-dark h2 { color: var(--paper); }
  .yk-dark .yk-grid3 { margin-top: 28px; }
  .yk-dark dt { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
                text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ochre-light); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .yk-dark dd { margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* ---- final + footer -------------------------------------------------- */
  .yk-final { text-align: center; padding: 88px 0 0; }
  .yk-final .yk-logo { width: 34px; height: 34px; margin: 0 auto 20px; border-radius: 8px; }
  .yk-final h2 { max-width: 20ch; margin: 0 auto; }
  .yk-final .yk-ctas { justify-content: center; }
  .yk-foot { margin-top: 88px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); padding: 22px 0 40px;
             display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; justify-content: space-between;
             font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--faint); }
  .yk-foot a { color: var(--faint); border-bottom-color: rgba(138, 133, 124, 0.35); }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .yk-nav-links a { display: none; }
    .yk-dark { padding: 28px 22px; }
  }
</style>

<div class="yk">

  <nav class="yk-nav">
    <div class="yk-col yk-nav-in">
      <a class="yk-brand" href="#top"><span class="yk-logo"><i></i><i></i></span><span class="yk-word">YAIkes</span></a>
      <div class="yk-nav-links">
        <a href="#how">How it works</a>
        <a href="#icks">Your icks</a>
        <a href="#privacy">Privacy</a>
      </div>
      {% if yaikesStoreUrl %}
      <a class="yk-btn yk-btn-sm" href="{{ yaikesStoreUrl }}">Add to Chrome →</a>
      {% else %}
      <span class="yk-btn-wait yk-btn-sm">in review</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- hero -->
  <header class="yk-col yk-hero" id="top">
    <p class="yk-over">Browser extension · runs on device · free</p>
    <h1>Your feed, minus the posts you already know you hate.</h1>
    <p class="yk-lead">YAIkes reads your feed so it doesn't have to show you all of it.
      Engagement bait, humblebrags, crypto shilling — you name the ick, it quietly folds
      those posts away and leaves a one-line receipt where each one stood.</p>
    <div class="yk-ctas">
      {% if yaikesStoreUrl %}
      <a class="yk-btn" href="{{ yaikesStoreUrl }}">Add to Chrome</a>
      {% else %}
      <span class="yk-btn-wait">Not on the Chrome Web Store yet</span>
      {% endif %}
      <span class="yk-note">free · no account · no server</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- hero screenshot -->
  <div class="yk-col" style="padding-top:44px;">
    <div class="yk-frame">
      <div class="yk-bar">
        <i class="yk-dot"></i><i class="yk-dot"></i><i class="yk-dot"></i>
        <span class="yk-mono">a feed, after</span>
      </div>
      <img src="/public/images/yaikes/collapsed-post.png"
           alt="A professional feed with one post collapsed to a single line reading: Hidden, close match for Engagement bait, with an Undo control." />
    </div>
    <p class="yk-cap">The post is gone. The receipt stays:
      <span class="yk-ochre">Hidden · close match for Engagement bait · Undo</span>.
      Nothing disappears without a paper trail.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- §1 -->
  <section class="yk-col yk-sec" id="how">
    <p class="yk-label">§1 — how it works</p>
    <h2>Three moves, all reversible</h2>
    <div class="yk-grid3">
      <div class="yk-card">
        <span class="yk-dia yk-dia-fill"></span>
        <h3>It hides the obvious ones</h3>
        <p>When a post is a <span class="yk-mono yk-ochre">close match</span> for one of your
          icks, it collapses to a single mono line naming the reason. One click undoes it —
          and teaches the filter it was wrong.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="yk-card">
        <span class="yk-dia yk-dia-out"></span>
        <h3>It asks about the borderline ones</h3>
        <p>A <span class="yk-mono yk-slate">possible</span> match stays visible. A quiet band
          appears under the post: hide these, or not this. Ochre means it acted; slate means
          it's asking. It never guesses in silence.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="yk-card">
        <span class="yk-circles"><i></i><i></i></span>
        <h3>You name the patterns</h3>
        <p>When several hidden posts smell alike, YAIkes shows you the evidence and an empty
          name field. You label the cluster — or dismiss it. It asks once, then drops it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- §2 -->
  <section class="yk-col yk-sec">
    <p class="yk-label">§2 — the review band</p>
    <div class="yk-two">
      <div>
        <h2>Asking looks different from acting</h2>
        <p>Confidence is exactly two words. <span class="yk-mono yk-ochre">close match</span>
          means it hid the post and you can undo. <span class="yk-mono yk-slate">possible</span>
          means the post stays put and the decision is yours. No scores, no percentages, no
          dashboard.</p>
        <p>“Not this” is a real answer — it whitelists the post and sharpens the pattern.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="yk-frame yk-frame-sm">
        <img src="/public/images/yaikes/review-band.png"
             alt="A post left visible with a quiet band beneath it reading possible, Engagement bait, offering Hide these or Not this." />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- §3 -->
  <section class="yk-col yk-sec" id="icks">
    <p class="yk-label">§3 — the popup</p>
    <div class="yk-two">
      <div class="yk-frame yk-frame-sm">
        <img src="/public/images/yaikes/your-icks.png"
             alt="The YAIkes popup: a list of icks with checkboxes, and three fields for adding your own." />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Your icks, in your words</h2>
        <p>Start with the classics — engagement bait, humblebrag, crypto shilling, hiring spam
          — and switch off any you secretly enjoy. Then add your own: describe an ick in plain
          language, paste an exact phrase, or block a link domain.</p>
        <p>The whole settings surface is one 280px popup. There is no onboarding, no tour, and
          nothing to configure that isn't a thing you'd rather not see.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- §4 -->
  <section class="yk-col yk-sec">
    <p class="yk-label">§4 — everywhere you scroll</p>
    <h2>Same manners on every feed</h2>
    <p class="yk-lead" style="margin-top:14px;">Long-form professional feeds, short-form
      timelines — the mark, the two words, and the receipt behave identically. Learn it once,
      trust it everywhere.</p>
    <div class="yk-frame" style="margin-top:26px;">
      <img src="/public/images/yaikes/short-form.png"
           alt="A short-form timeline with the same review band beneath the first post." />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- §5 -->
  <section class="yk-col yk-sec" id="privacy">
    <p class="yk-label">§5 — privacy</p>
    <div class="yk-dark">
      <h2>Your feed never leaves your machine</h2>
      <dl class="yk-grid3">
        <div>
          <dt>on device</dt>
          <dd>Detection runs locally. No post text, author, or URL is ever sent anywhere.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>no account</dt>
          <dd>Nothing to sign up for. Your icks live in local extension storage, and removing
            the extension removes all of it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>no server</dt>
          <dd>The model ships inside the extension. There is no backend to breach, because
            there is no backend — the extension never makes a network request of its own.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p style="margin-top:24px;font-size:14.5px;">
        <strong style="color:var(--paper);font-weight:600;">YAIkes is closed source.</strong>
        Saying so plainly matters more than the claim it replaces: the design for this page
        advertised an open-source project, and it is not one. You cannot read the repository.
        What you <em>can</em> check, without taking anyone's word for it, is the extension you
        actually installed — open your browser's network tab and watch it make no requests,
        read the permissions it asks for on the store listing, and unpack the extension itself,
        which ships as ordinary unobfuscated JavaScript.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:14.5px;">
        <a href="/yaikes-privacy/" style="color:var(--ochre-light);border-bottom-color:oklch(0.75 0.11 62 / 0.4);">Read
        the privacy policy</a> — it lists every stored key and what is in it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- final -->
  <section class="yk-col yk-final">
    <span class="yk-logo"><i></i><i></i></span>
    <h2>Install it, name three icks, scroll in peace.</h2>
    <div class="yk-ctas">
      {% if yaikesStoreUrl %}
      <a class="yk-btn" href="{{ yaikesStoreUrl }}">Add to Chrome →</a>
      {% else %}
      <span class="yk-btn-wait">Chrome Web Store listing pending review</span>
      {% endif %}
      <a class="yk-btn yk-btn-out" href="{{ supportUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Buy me a coffee →</a>
    </div>
    <p class="yk-note" style="margin-top:18px;">Free, all of it. The coffee unlocks nothing.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="yk-col">
    <div class="yk-foot">
      <span>YAIkes — yet another ick spotter</span>
      <span>screens are mock feeds · no real platform harmed</span>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
